            "Administrators can manage users, system settings, integrations, plate matching profiles, and recurring aliases when the related permission is present.",
            "System Logs is available to Administrators and Auditors. It shows the bounded active application log newest first. Filters are collapsed by default so more entries remain visible; expand Filters for log level, component, camera, request ID, read ID, time range, full-field search, and rows-per-page controls. The compact toolbar summarizes active filters and keeps Refresh available. Live updating is enabled by default and refreshes the newest page every five seconds; it pauses on older pages, while the browser tab is hidden, whenever any log entry is expanded for JSON inspection, or while a durable read timeline is open, then resumes automatically. The Live control can also pause or resume updates manually. Collapsed entries remain one line; when space permits, Blue Iris rows keep only the camera, trigger type received from &TYPE, evaluated direction, and first read ID inline. Select a row to reveal secondary component, request, direction-error, and additional-read tags with sanitized JSON immediately below. Each tag highlights its exact JSON field. The copy action works on both HTTPS and direct-LAN HTTP installations, and plate-ingress rows provide a receipt action that filters Ingress Receipts by the same request ID and opens its first match. When Logs is opened for a specific read, the compact Durable read timeline separates persistent read, direction, notification-handoff, Vehicle View, and legacy Pushover outcomes from rotating operational logs. The timeline is collapsed by default, contains only allowlisted non-sensitive outcome evidence, and begins with reads accepted after this release; older reads continue to show their available operational logs and ingress receipts.",
            "Ingress Receipts is available beside Operational Logs to Administrators and Auditors. It retains bounded metadata rather than request values. Expand a receipt to see its schema version, recognized field names, trigger aliases, whether aliases conflicted, large-field size summaries, and body fingerprint. Request and read log actions filter Operational Logs to the correlated evidence and open its first JSON row; the request-ID copy action also supports direct-LAN HTTP. Produced reads and duplicate-target read IDs link to the exact Recognition Feed record and their operational logs. Alias diagnostics never expose alternate trigger values, and receipts never store API keys, plate values, request bodies, images, AI dumps, or Blue Iris paths.",
            "Retention & incidents is available beside Operational Logs and Ingress Receipts. Administrators and Auditors can review operational-file, receipt, read-timeline, and hot/archive audit growth and export existing incident packages. An Administrator can protect one request ID, one read ID, or a time window of at most seven days; Protect and snapshot immediately captures a bounded immutable JSON evidence package and excludes matching live receipt and audit rows from retention until the displayed protection date. The package itself remains append-only after protection expires. Cleanup never runs on a schedule: Create retention preview changes nothing, is valid for 15 minutes and only for the same Administrator, and lists the exact expired receipt and old audit rows. Type ARCHIVE LOG EVIDENCE to execute that exact preview. Old audit rows are copied and verified in the immutable partitioned archive before leaving the hot table; expired receipts are then removed. If the candidate set changes, the preview is invalidated and no evidence is changed. Read-timeline retention continues to follow the parent read lifecycle, while operational and PostgreSQL container logs use bounded file rotation.",
