            "Administrators can open Settings > Data & Privacy and use the Storage Health, Monitoring, Cleanup, and Privacy tabs. Each tab has a clean address that can be bookmarked or restored with browser navigation.",
            "Storage Health contains capacity, category, database, capture, visual-index, projection, and read-only PostgreSQL statistics. Monitoring contains thresholds, scheduler liveness, reconciliation, and alert destinations. Cleanup contains derived-orphan and host-retention controls. Privacy contains the local-only reporting and explicit-integration policy.",
            "Mounted filesystem capacity and PostgreSQL size are direct measurements. Completed reconciliation provides exact source-image, thumbnail, and derived-file counts and bytes. Docker and backup totals appear only from a current read-only host snapshot and otherwise remain clearly unavailable.",
            "Reads/day uses the last seven days. Estimated bytes/read samples at most 120 recent source, thumbnail, and derived files; it does not recursively scan the storage tree.",
