            "An automatic run handles at most 100 files or 1 GiB and admits new candidates for at most five minutes, without catch-up loops. Per-candidate database lock and statement waits use the remaining scheduling budget; a filesystem operation already in progress is allowed to finish safely. It rechecks the current approval revision between files and uses the same five-column reference, advisory/writer lock, table lock, real-path, symlink, hard-link, size, mtime, device, and inode safeguards as manual cleanup. A failure suspends automation, makes reconciliation due, and requires a newer successful reconciliation plus typed Administrator acknowledgement.",
