            "The database-backup button remains disabled when that exact worker capability is absent or stale. Shipping the application control plane alone does not install the reviewed fixed adapter, runtime tooling, approved backup-root implementation, or verification receipt. The reviewed worker is active and capability-validated on staging and production. On August 2, the first authorized production request completed once and verified alpr-postgres-20260802T164636Z-1.dump at 61.8 MB with no reported error. The worker role has only narrow access to the dedicated request queue; the fixed host adapter performs the dump against the exact database container.",
            "All host schedules default off. Docker cache and backup retention require different one-time activation phrases. Unused-image scheduling is unsupported, and backup cleanup never deletes images. The manual image-retirement grace defaults to seven days and can be changed from one to 365 days only with Administrator approval and the displayed typed phrase. Application and maintenance-worker images use separate append-only ledgers, and the current attested worker is protected. A reviewed worker may adopt only exact, verifiable legacy identities where rollback references are fully accounted for; unknown production application images remain protected and block preview. If the worker is not installed or its heartbeat is stale, the controls fail closed and a rate-limited maintenance alert is raised when scheduled work depends on it.",
            "When a host category's safety breaker is open, an Administrator with automatic-cleanup approval permission must type that category's displayed acknowledgement phrase. The server locks the current breaker and accepts acknowledgement only when the failed destructive receipt belongs to that breaker and a newer healthy worker heartbeat and inventory exist. Success appends immutable actor and worker evidence, closes only that breaker, keeps every host schedule disabled, deletes nothing, and requires a separately queued read-only preview before any cleanup request.",
            "Backup retention always protects the newest five verified backups and every verified backup newer than 30 days, plus current and rollback chains. The worker rejects partial, corrupt, foreign, manifestless, symbolic-link, hard-link, or identity-drifted backups. Current/prepared releases, the exactly attested current maintenance worker, database data, captures, volumes, container references, leases, and unknown images remain protected. An environment-specific worker installation may append exact pre-control-plane identities as retired metadata only when immutable labels match and rollback references are fully accounted for; production leaves unknown application images protected. Adoption deletes nothing and starts the configured grace.",
            "An unused-image preview reports the logical size of eligible image identities for cap enforcement; it is not a promise of filesystem space. After each exact deletion, the locked worker measures Docker's layer-store size before and after the operation and reports only the conservative Docker-accounted decrease, capped by that candidate's logical size. Shared layers can therefore make actual reported reclaim smaller than the preview, including zero.",
